Z||000000||Phil||06-19-2000||08:48 AM||||Whew! Three weeks in a Fiero (Coast to Coast to Coast) RI to CA to FL to RI- 8135 miles. Had a great time meeting fellow car lovers along the way. Even met some Forum Folks who stopped by to say hi. Unfortunately only saw 3 other Fieros on the tour and only for one or two days. It was interesting to see how much attention a Fiero still gets even though being surrounded by about 1000-1500 hot rods,  muscle cars, classics and the like. A special thanks to the members of Gulf Coast Fieros (FL) They invited me to a little bash/meeting they were having. They met us at a rest area and we had a mini cruise (about 10 Fieros) to free eats and a good time. Of course you can't stop this car stuff cold turkey so on the way home from Fl to RI had to stop at the Williamsburg VA  Fiero to-do, another great time. But for now I Fiero-ed out(but July stuff is coming) Now I can sit back and catch up on all the new posts.||||reg||1
